{
  "kanda": "kishkindha",
  "sarga": 47,
  "title": "Search for Seetha failed in east, north, and west",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga47/kishkindhasans47.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga47/kishkindhaitrans47.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Search for Seetha failed in east, north, and west directions. The monkey chiefs who went there have come back to inform that she is not found and they all hoped Hanuma to find her out, because he is pursuing the direction in which Seetha was taken away."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे सप्त चत्वारिन्शः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 47th chapter in Kishkindha Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "4.47.1",
      "label": "4.47.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "दर्शनार्थम् तु वैदेह्याः सर्वतः कपि कुंजराः |\nव्यादिष्टाः कपि राजेन यथा उक्तम् जग्मुर् अंजसा",
